cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset or code, please cite as below."
title: "AgroSense: Satellite-Based Crop Stress Classification for Pakistan"
authors:
  - family-names: Shahmeer
    given-names: Ali
    orcid: ""
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2024-08-19"
url: "https://github.com/ALI-SHAHMEER/agrosense-pakistan-crop-stress"
abstract: >
  AgroSense is a crop stress classification system that uses Sentinel-2
  satellite imagery collected via the Google Earth Engine API to classify
  Pakistani agricultural fields into Healthy, Stressed, or Diseased states.
  This repository contains 1,786 real Sentinel-2 observations from 116 field
  sites across all four provinces of Pakistan over ten growing seasons
  (2015-2024), along with the training code for five ML classifiers.
keywords:
  - remote sensing
  - precision agriculture
  - crop stress
  - Sentinel-2
  - machine learning
  - Pakistan
  - Google Earth Engine
